---
// Markup as published by the Webflow build (ported 2026-11-18).
---

<section
  id="parallax"
  data-motion="lesson"
  data-theme="color"
  data-wf--lesson-section--variant="parallax"
  class="lesson-section w-variant-535a4d56-ec86-2bf1-7fa5-1086a8c482f7"
>
  <div class="lesson-hero">
    <div aria-hidden="true" class="lesson-visual-row">
      <div class="lesson-star is-left"></div>
      <div data-src="/assets/Parallax-f46a.json" data-motion="lesson-visual" data-kind="lottie" class="lesson-visual"></div>
      <div class="lesson-star is-right"></div>
    </div>
    <div class="lesson-head">
      <div class="lesson-heading">
        <div class="lesson-number"><div class="heading-md">7</div></div>
        <div class="lesson-title"><h2 class="heading-md">Parallax</h2></div>
      </div>
      <div class="lesson-desc">
        <p class="body-md">
          Arranged in layers, several objects pass simultaneously through x and y axes: the farther the object, the less it passes. The result is a feeling of
          space.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div></div>
  <div data-motion="lesson-cases" class="lesson-cases">
    <div data-motion="lesson-cases-head" class="lesson-cases-head"><h3 class="heading-xl">Implementation examples</h3></div>
    <div class="lesson-cases-pin">
      <div data-motion="lesson-track" class="lesson-cases-track">
        <a data-motion="lesson-card" href="https://dribbble.com/shots/19663094-Milkinside-wallet-iOS-app" target="_blank" class="lesson-card w-inline-block"
          ><div class="lesson-card-media">
            <video
              data-motion="lesson-video"
              data-src="https://cdn.zajno.com/dev/motion/videos/Lessons/lesson-7/milkinside_desktop_H.264.mp4"
              muted=""
              loop=""
              playsinline="playsinline"
              preload="none"
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="lesson-card-video"
            ></video
            ><img src="/assets/milkinside_desktop_00000.png" loading="lazy" alt="" class="lesson-card-poster" />
          </div>
          <div class="lesson-card-body">
            <div class="lesson-card-text">
              <p class="body-sm">
                As the matte translucent object with the chart and other information moves upwards, the cards underneath it subtly shift position. This
                &#x27;parallax effect&#x27; supports the main 3D visualization.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="lesson-card-btn">
              <div>View</div>
              <div class="lesson-card-icon w-embed">
                <svg width="100%" height="100%" viewBox="0 0 13 25" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M0.5 12.1338H11.5M11.5 12.1338L8.15217 9.13379M11.5 12.1338L8.15217 15.1338" stroke="currentColor" />
                </svg>
              </div>
            </div></div></a
        ><a data-motion="lesson-card" href="https://dribbble.com/shots/13961411-Breathtaking" target="_blank" class="lesson-card w-inline-block"
          ><div class="lesson-card-media">
            <video
              data-motion="lesson-video"
              data-src="https://cdn.zajno.com/dev/motion/videos/Lessons/lesson-7/breathtaking_desktop_H.264.mp4"
              muted=""
              loop=""
              playsinline="playsinline"
              preload="none"
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="lesson-card-video"
            ></video
            ><img src="/assets/breathtaking_desktop_00000.png" loading="lazy" alt="" class="lesson-card-poster" />
          </div>
          <div class="lesson-card-body">
            <div class="lesson-card-text">
              <p class="body-sm">
                A classic use of parallax sees an in-focus foreground move in relation to the out-of-focus scenery beyond – just like the view the runner sees.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="lesson-card-btn">
              <div>View</div>
              <div class="lesson-card-icon w-embed">
                <svg width="100%" height="100%" viewBox="0 0 13 25" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M0.5 12.1338H11.5M11.5 12.1338L8.15217 9.13379M11.5 12.1338L8.15217 15.1338" stroke="currentColor" />
                </svg>
              </div>
            </div></div></a
        ><a data-motion="lesson-card" href="https://dribbble.com/shots/19956284-The-Ways-We-Work" target="_blank" class="lesson-card w-inline-block"
          ><div class="lesson-card-media">
            <video
              data-motion="lesson-video"
              data-src="https://cdn.zajno.com/dev/motion/videos/Lessons/lesson-7/The Ways We Work_desktop_H.264.mp4"
              muted=""
              loop=""
              playsinline="playsinline"
              preload="none"
              aria-hidden="true"
              class="lesson-card-video"
            ></video
            ><img src="/assets/The-Ways-We-Work_desktop_00000.png" loading="lazy" alt="" class="lesson-card-poster" />
          </div>
          <div class="lesson-card-body">
            <div class="lesson-card-text">
              <p class="body-sm">
                In interactive parallax, movements of the mouse trigger slight displacement of objects on screen – a stylish finishing touch for a minimalistic
                design.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="lesson-card-btn">
              <div>View</div>
              <div class="lesson-card-icon w-embed">
                <svg width="100%" height="100%" viewBox="0 0 13 25" fill="none" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" aria-hidden="true">
                  <path d="M0.5 12.1338H11.5M11.5 12.1338L8.15217 9.13379M11.5 12.1338L8.15217 15.1338" stroke="currentColor" />
                </svg>
              </div>
            </div></div
        ></a>
      </div>
    </div>
    <div aria-hidden="true" data-motion="lesson-overlay" class="lesson-cases-overlay"></div>
  </div>
  <div></div>
</section>
